# New-world setup popup and settings notes. Keys are relative to Mods.Levy.Setup.
Title: Set up your army
Intro: Pick how many levies you field and how bosses treat them. Everything can be changed later in the Levy config.
Button: Setup
ButtonHint: Reopen the world setup. Also /levysetup.
CommandHelp: Reopen the Levy world setup.
Skip: Skip for now
SkipHint: Keep the current settings. Reopen any time with /levysetup.
Customize: Customize
CustomizeHint: Set the levy counts and boss behaviour yourself.
Apply: Apply
ApplyHint: Save these settings.
Back: Back
StepHint: Shift changes it by 5.
MoreOptions: Every other option is under Settings, Mod Configuration, Levy.
HostOnly: Only the host of a single player world can change the Levy setup. Use the mod config.
Done: "{0} settings applied."
DoneCustom: Your settings are applied.
Skipped: Setup skipped. Type /levysetup to reopen it.
Anchors: Levies start at {0}. Pre-hardmode bosses carry you to {1} at the Wall of Flesh. Hardmode bosses carry you to {2} at Moon Lord. Every boss after Moon Lord adds the last {3}.
CountStart: At the start: {0}  (recommended {1} to {2})
CountPre: By the Wall of Flesh: {0}  (recommended {1} to {2})
CountHardmode: By Moon Lord: {0}  (recommended {1} to {2})
CountPost: By the final boss: {0}  (recommended {1} to {2})
TargetOn: Bosses you have beaten target levies on rematches
TargetOff: Bosses never target levies
PunishOn: Bosses punish levies that get close
PunishOff: Bosses ignore levies that get close
TargetHint: Bosses you have already beaten chase the nearest levy like a player. A first kill is always solo.
PunishHint: Bosses redirect shots and dashes at levies that get close or hurt them.
PresetNumbers: Levies: {0} / {1} / {2} / {3}

Preset: {
	Default: Default
	DefaultBlurb: The standard army. Bosses punish levies that get close and never chase them.
	Relaxed: Relaxed
	RelaxedBlurb: More levies. Bosses never target them.
	Hardcore: Hardcore
	HardcoreBlurb: Fewer levies. Bosses you have beaten target levies on rematches.
}

Warn: {
	StartFew: Too few levies at the start. Early game will feel lonely.
	StartAbovePre: The starting levies are above the Wall of Flesh count. The count holds until hardmode.
	PreFew: Too few levies by the Wall of Flesh. Early bosses will feel lonely.
	PreMany: Too many levies by the Wall of Flesh. Early bosses will fall quickly.
	HardmodeFew: Too few levies by Moon Lord. Hardmode bosses will feel lonely.
	HardmodeMany: Too many levies by Moon Lord. Hardmode bosses will fall quickly.
	PostFew: Too few levies by the final boss. The last bosses will feel lonely.
	PostMany: Too many levies by the final boss. The last bosses will fall quickly.
	MaxBelowPost: The maximum levies is below the final-boss count. The maximum wins.
}
